<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <title>QR Code Security Demonstration</title>

  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background-color: #111;
      color: white;
      text-align: center;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 35px 20px;
    }

    .warning {
      font-size: 60px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 44px;
      margin: 10px 0;
    }

    .gotcha {
      color: #ff4444;
    }

    .message {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 30px auto;
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .safe {
      background-color: #ffffff;
      color: #111;
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 30px auto;
      padding: 25px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      font-size: 21px;
    }

    .lesson {
      font-size: 30px;
      margin-top: 35px;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .rule {
      font-size: 34px;
      margin-top: 25px;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 50px;
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #bbb;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <div class="warning">⚠️</div>

  <h1 class="gotcha">GOTCHA!</h1>

  <div class="message">
    You just scanned a QR code from someone you don't know.
  </div>

  <div class="safe">
    <strong>Don't worry — this demonstration is harmless.</strong>

    <p>
      Nothing has been installed on your phone and no information
      has been collected.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="message">
    But what if this page had looked like your bank's login page?
  </div>

  <div class="message">
    What if it asked for your password, credit card number,
    Social Security number, or verification code?
  </div>

  <div class="lesson">
    A QR code is just a link.
  </div>

  <div class="message">
    The problem is that you often don't know where that link
    will take you until you scan it.
  </div>

  <div class="rule">
    STOP → THINK → VERIFY
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    Adult Technology Security Demonstration
  </div>

</body>
</html>
